Q: How to get emf image as input stream from system clipboard? A: <p>Your code almost works as is. You just need to change <code>&quot;CF_METAFILEPICT&quot;</code> to <code>&quot;METAFILEPICT&quot;</code> (or <code>&quot;ENHMETAFILE&quot;</code>):</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>String clipboardName = &quot;METAFILEPICT&quot;;
Clipboard clipboard = Toolkit.getDefaultToolkit().getSystemClipboard();
SystemFlavorMap flavorMap = (SystemFlavorMap) SystemFlavorMap.getDefaultFlavorMap();
DataFlavor myDataFlavor = new DataFlavor(java.io.InputStream.class, &quot;&quot;);
flavorMap.addFlavorForUnencodedNative(clipboardName , myDataFlavor);
InputStream data = (InputStream) clipboard.getData(myDataFlavor);
</code></pre>
<p>(note that this will throw an <code>UnsupportedFlavorException</code> with no WMF present in the clipboard)</p>
<p>Java defines clipboard flavor &quot;native&quot; names for Windows here: <a href="https://github.com/openjdk/jdk/blob/a6db3f870218bc016ecc67e3f5e142d6491ac080/src/java.desktop/windows/classes/sun/awt/windows/WDataTransferer.java#L81-L100" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/openjdk/jdk/blob/a6db3f870218bc016ecc67e3f5e142d6491ac080/src/java.desktop/windows/classes/sun/awt/windows/WDataTransferer.java#L81-L100</a></p>

Q: SELECT SUM() of values in a single column for rows with a timestamp from last month with CodeIgniter&#39;s query builder A: <p>CodeIgniter's query builder can support what you need. Prepare the date range boundaries in PHP and the summing query will perform well.</p>
<p>I never recommend using <code>false</code> as a fallback return value from a model method when the return type is otherwise non-boolean.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function totalCountLastMonth(): int
{
    $start = date('Y-m-01 00:00:00', strtotime('first day of last month'));
    $end = date('Y-m-01 00:00:00'); // first day of this month

    return (int)$this-&gt;db
        -&gt;select_sum('count')
        -&gt;get_where('user_agent', ['timestamp &gt;=' =&gt; $start, 'timestamp &lt;' =&gt; $end])
        -&gt;row('count') ?? 0;
}
</code></pre>

