Q: How to get rid of whitespace between Runs in TextBlock? A: <p>If the only reason you want multiple runs is so you can bind to multiple values for a single <code>TextBlock</code>, you can instead use a <code>MultiBinding</code> with <code>StringFormat</code>:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;TextBlock
    FontFamily=&quot;Arial&quot;
    FontSize=&quot;10&quot;
    Foreground=&quot;#414141&quot;
    HorizontalAlignment=&quot;Center&quot;
    VerticalAlignment=&quot;Center&quot;&gt;
    &lt;TextBlock.Text&gt;
        &lt;MultiBinding StringFormat=&quot;{}{0}+{1}&quot;&gt;
            &lt;Binding Path=&quot;LoadsCount&quot;/&gt;
            &lt;Binding Path=&quot;BrokerLoadsCount&quot;/&gt;
        &lt;/MultiBinding&gt;
    &lt;/TextBlock.Text&gt;
&lt;/TextBlock&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>The <code>{}</code> in the beginning of the <code>StringFormat</code> is needed because the XAML parser would otherwise attempt to interpret <code>{0}</code> as a markup extension.</p>
<p>If you want localization (e.g. <code>&quot;{0} out of {1}&quot;</code>), you can also use <code>{x:Static local:Resources.MyResourceKey}</code> as the <code>StringFormat</code> to bind to localizable resources.</p>
